## SQ-DEP-05 | rain puts out an open-sky campfire on stone, not one on a coal block; the douse tag is present
@group A
@commands Same boot: `/setblock` a `minecraft:campfire` under open sky and one on a `minecraft:coal_block` beside it, `/weather thunder`, wait 400 ticks, then `/execute if block <pos> minecraft:campfire[lit=false]` for each; `/dumpall`, `grep -c "creativecommon:campfire/rain_douses" kubejs/exported/tags/block_tags.json`
@pass open-sky campfire out, the one on coal lit; tag present (1)
@fails Common's `CampfireRainInfo` namespace vs `block_dict.js` `t_campfire_rain_*` (7.17 item 1)
@jars creativebrewing creativecommon creativedelight creativedevtools creativeengineering creativemagic
@sources feature_writeup/creative_split.md
@tier T2
@reviewed 2026-11-20
@from batches/r1113/c2_a1.qb
# forceload (r1120fix, 2026-11-20): r1120nv batch fault, the campfire area was not loaded
> forceload add 328 296 336 304
sleep 3
> setblock 330 -61 300 minecraft:stone
> setblock 330 -60 300 minecraft:campfire[lit=true]
> setblock 332 -61 300 minecraft:coal_block
> setblock 332 -60 300 minecraft:campfire[lit=true]
> weather thunder
> cdevtest tickwarp 400
waitlog verb=tickwarp end= 60
expect verb=tickwarp end=done ticks=400
> execute if block 330 -60 300 minecraft:campfire[lit=false]
> execute if block 332 -60 300 minecraft:campfire[lit=true]
> cdevtest tag block creativecommon:campfire/rain_douses
> weather clear
count Test passed == 2
expect verb=tag kind=block tag=creativecommon:campfire/rain_douses n=[1-9]
reject \[cdevtest\] .*done=0
look the row's /dumpall grep is replaced by the live tag query (same tag)

## SQ-DNR-O-02 | 
@group A
@commands Eat Shrimp Stew, Bowl of Paella, Sea Grape, Sea Grape Juice and Nautilus Juice; use the paella and pufferfish with and without a bowl; knife the sponge cake, then eat from it; bone meal a sea grape plant; brew Awkward + Elder Guardian Eye, then + redstone, + glowstone
@pass Bowls, bottle and shell come back; Comfort 4:00 (paella), Nourishment 4:00 (shrimp stew) by the pack rule (upstream 5:00), Instant Breath (air full) apply, with blue tooltip lines; no bowl gives "You need a Bowl to eat this."; the empty paella pan is picked up (pan + skillet); a slice drops; bone meal adds a plant; the three Mining Fatigue potions brew and JEI shows them
@fails Compare with ocean_delight.md 5.6; missing effect: Farmer's Delight effect id lookup in `OceanicFood.farmers`
@jars creativedelight
@sources feature_writeup/creative_delight.md feature_writeup/ocean_delight.md feature_writeup/ends_delight.md
@tier T2
@reviewed 2026-11-20
> forceload add 2592 2592 2616 2616
> pbot spawn dnr2 2600 -60 2600 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 3
> clear dnr2
> effect clear dnr2
> pbot hunger dnr2 4
> pbot hold dnr2 oceanic_delight:shrimp_stew
> pbot eat dnr2
sleep 4
> cdevtest player dnr2
> effect clear dnr2
> pbot hunger dnr2 4
> pbot hold dnr2 oceanic_delight:bowl_of_paella
> pbot eat dnr2
sleep 4
> cdevtest player dnr2
> effect clear dnr2
> pbot hunger dnr2 4
> pbot hold dnr2 oceanic_delight:sea_grape
> pbot eat dnr2
sleep 4
> cdevtest player dnr2
> effect clear dnr2
> pbot hunger dnr2 4
> pbot hold dnr2 oceanic_delight:sea_grape_juice
> pbot eat dnr2
sleep 4
> cdevtest player dnr2
> effect clear dnr2
> pbot hunger dnr2 4
> pbot hold dnr2 oceanic_delight:nautilus_juice
> pbot eat dnr2
sleep 4
> cdevtest player dnr2
> pbot inv dnr2 get
count verb=pbot.useitem bot=dnr2 end=finish == 5
# r1120fix (2026-11-20): the pack Comfort / Nourishment rule (comfort_nourishment.md 10; comfort_nourishment.json set:
# shrimp_stew nourishment 240 s, bowl_of_paella comfort 240 s) gives 4:00, not upstream 5:00; the containers are read
# from the useitem result (each pbot hold overwrites slot 0, so the inventory keeps only the last one)
expect verb=player name=dnr2 effects=\S*farmersdelight:comfort:0:4[5-8]\d\d\b
expect verb=player name=dnr2 effects=\S*farmersdelight:nourishment:0:4[5-8]\d\d\b
count verb=pbot.useitem bot=dnr2 end=finish item=oceanic_delight:(shrimp_stew|bowl_of_paella)\S* result=minecraft:bowl == 2
expect verb=pbot.useitem bot=dnr2 end=finish item=oceanic_delight:sea_grape_juice\S* result=minecraft:glass_bottle
expect verb=pbot.useitem bot=dnr2 end=finish item=oceanic_delight:nautilus_juice\S* result=minecraft:nautilus_shell
> pbot remove dnr2
> cdevtest place 2604 -60 2604 oceanic_delight:paella_plate
> cdevtest use 2604 -60 2604 held=minecraft:bowl hand=main
> cdevtest place 2606 -60 2604 oceanic_delight:sponge_cake
> cdevtest use 2606 -60 2604 held=farmersdelight:flint_knife hand=main
> cdevtest items 2606 -60 2604 2
> cdevtest place 2608 -61 2604 minecraft:sand
> fill 2607 -60 2603 2609 -58 2605 minecraft:water
> cdevtest place 2608 -60 2604 oceanic_delight:sea_grape_plant
> cdevtest use 2608 -60 2604 held=minecraft:bone_meal hand=main
> cdevtest count 2608 -60 2604 2608 -55 2604 oceanic_delight:sea_grape_plant
> cdevtest potion minecraft:awkward oceanic_delight:elder_guardian_eye
> cdevtest potion oceanic_delight:mining_fatigue minecraft:redstone,minecraft:glowstone_dust
expect verb=use main=oceanic_delight:bowl_of_paella\*1
expect verb=items items=\S*oceanic_delight:sponge_cake_slice:1\b
expect verb=potion potion=minecraft:awkward ingredient=oceanic_delight:elder_guardian_eye output="minecraft:potion oceanic_delight:mining_fatigue"
expect verb=potion potion=oceanic_delight:mining_fatigue ingredient=minecraft:redstone output="minecraft:potion oceanic_delight:mining_fatigue_extended"
expect verb=potion potion=oceanic_delight:mining_fatigue ingredient=minecraft:glowstone_dust output="minecraft:potion oceanic_delight:mining_fatigue_two"
reject (\[cdevtest\] .*done=0|verb=pbot\.\S+ .*error=|Unknown item|No player was found)
look the five player lines: Comfort 4:00, Nourishment 4:00, Instant Breath (air=300) after the right food; the sea grape count above 1 after the bone meal; the empty paella pan pick-up (pan + skillet), the "You need a Bowl" message, the blue tooltip lines and JEI are client (CQ)

## SQ-DRK-01 | drink scripts load clean; 14 items and 17 fluids registered
@group A
@commands Boot; `grep -nE "Error occurred while handling event\|drinks.js\|drink_tags.js\|kettle.js" logs/latest.log logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/kubejs/server.log \| head -30`; `grep -n "\[NCH\]" logs/kubejs/server.log \| grep -iE "tea\|juice\|coffee\|latte\|nectar" \| head`
@pass No error; no NCH warning naming a drink; no duplicate recipe id; startup registers the 14 items and 17 fluids (`/give @p creativeengineering:kiwi_tea`, `creativeengineering:peach_juice` work)
@fails missing dict key (`item_dict.js` / `fluid_dict.js` not updated on the server), duplicate id with `kettle.js` or a member file
@jars creativedelight
@sources feature_writeup/creative_delight_drinks.md
@tier T2
@reviewed 2026-11-20
@from batches/r1102b/s5_A.qb
shell ! grep -iE '(error|exception).*(drinks|drink_tags|kettle|fluids)\.js' logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/kubejs/server.log
shell ! (grep -n 'Error occurred while handling event' logs/latest.log | grep -qiE 'drink|kettle|tea|juice')
kjsreject \[NCH\].*(?i:tea|juice|coffee|latte|nectar)
kjsreject (?i)duplicate recipe id
# own home (r1120fix, 2026-11-20): {S5H} came from the retired r1103 home batches; rows run alone with --rows
> execute unless entity @e[type=minecraft:marker,tag=s5home] run summon minecraft:marker ~ ~ ~ {Tags:["s5home"]}
sleep 2
> data get entity @e[type=minecraft:marker,tag=s5home,limit=1] Pos
capture S5H entity data: \[(-?\d+)\.\d+d, (-?\d+)\.\d+d, (-?\d+)\.\d+d\]
> forceload add {S5H1+16} {S5H3+28} {S5H1+20} {S5H3+32}
sleep 3
> pbot spawn s5g {S5H1+18} {S5H2} {S5H3+30} minecraft:overworld survival
